TITLE:: RCAttractor
summary:: A discrete set a coordinate is drawn to: courses that linger near its values
categories:: Libraries>reCurrent
related:: Classes/RCCurve, Classes/RCLines, Classes/RCSieve

DESCRIPTION::
A set of values (a scale's pitches, a sieve, chosen directions or levels) a voice's course is drawn to: the course lingers near the values and passes quickly between them, from even glides (strong::amount:: 0) to nearly steps (1).

For consecutive attractors a < b with weights wa and wb, a value x between them becomes code::a + (b - a) S(u)::, with code::u = (x - a) / (b - a)::, code::S(u) = (tanh(s (u - m)) + tanh(s m)) / (tanh(s (1 - m)) + tanh(s m))::, code::m = wa / (wa + wb):: and the strength code::s = 40^amount - 1::. The warp is monotone and fixes every attractor. As s grows it flattens near the attractors and steepens between them, so an evenly moving value lingers near each attractor. The switch between two neighbours moves towards the lighter one (a weight of 0 never holds).

Two modes:
list::
## strong::value::: a coordinate is warped, its course straight or curved, through a gliding release too (link::#*kr::);
## strong::time::: a line's index is warped (link::Classes/RCCurve#*course:: reads every coordinate at it), so the whole voice slows near the set and keeps its ends. A straight driving coordinate warps through the set itself (link::#-progressAt::), a curved one through the progress values where it crosses the attractors (link::#-crossings::) (link::#*progress::).
::

A set repeats every strong::period:: from a strong::root:: (an octave for a scale), or not at all (link::#*values::: outside its span a value is left as it is). A synth holds link::#*maxDegrees:: values per period (with a period on each side); a periodic set too large is cut to what each line reaches.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: degrees
The values: of one period from root when period > 0 (reduced into it), absolute otherwise.
argument:: period
argument:: root
argument:: weights
One per degree, in the degrees' order (1 by default).
argument:: name

METHOD:: periodic
argument:: degrees
argument:: period
argument:: root
argument:: weights
argument:: name

METHOD:: values
Absolute values that do not repeat.
argument:: values
argument:: weights
argument:: name

METHOD:: edo
strong::n:: equal divisions of the period (an octave by default) from root.
argument:: n
argument:: root
argument:: period
argument:: weights

METHOD:: scale
A link::Classes/Scale::, a link::Classes/Tuning::, or a Symbol naming one: its degrees in octaves, its period the octave ratio's log2 (through link::Classes/RCSieve#*tuningSteps::); an Array of values gives a set that does not repeat.
argument:: scale
argument:: root
argument:: weights

METHOD:: sieve
An link::Classes/RCSieve::: its points over one period from its zero (the formula's period times its unit; for a tuned sieve, the period after which formula and tuning repeat together); a tuned sieve on a fixed field gives its points, not repeating.
argument:: sieve
argument:: weights
argument:: name

METHOD:: from
An attractor from what a spec names: an RCAttractor, an RCSieve, a Scale, a Tuning or a Symbol naming one, an Integer (equal divisions of the octave), an Array (values); nil otherwise.
argument:: thing

METHOD:: strength
code::40^amount - 1::.
argument:: amount

METHOD:: shape
S(u) for strength s and switch point m.
argument:: u
argument:: s
argument:: m

METHOD:: mid
The switch point of two weights (0.5 when both are 0).
argument:: wa
argument:: wb

METHOD:: maxDegrees
Values per period a synth holds (32).

METHOD:: maxCrossings
Progress values a curved line's time warp holds, its ends included (64).

subsection:: In a SynthDef

METHOD:: kr
A coordinate's value warped by its attractor: the controls code::<key>_astr:: (the strength, 0: none), code::<key>_aset:: (what a LocalBuf holds, filled when the synth starts), code::<key>_aweights::, code::<key>_an::, code::<key>_aperiod:: (0: not repeating), code::<key>_aroot::. Searched by link::Classes/IndexInBetween::; the value as it is when the strength is 0 or outside a set that does not repeat.
argument:: key
argument:: x

METHOD:: progress
The time warp of a line's index (0 → 1 over the line, left as it is past 1): the controls code::progress_*:: hold the driving course's set, its ends code::progress_x0:: and code::_x1:: and the warp at them, code::_aw0:: and code::_aw1:: (a curved course: its crossings, x0 0, x1 1, W 0 and 1).
argument:: index

METHOD:: controls
The NamedControls of a key's attractor, an Event.
argument:: key
argument:: size

subsection:: In a template

METHOD:: resolve
What a hit's spec, an Event key → code::(set:, amount:, mode: \value | \time | \both, weights:)::, with code::time_key:: (the key driving the time mode, code::\pitch:: by default), asks of strong::keys::: code::[[[key, set, amount], ...], [key, set, amount]]::, the keys warped and the key driving the time mode (nil when none). A key counts with a set of at least one value and an amount above 0; the time mode goes to code::time_key:: when it asks for it, else to the first key that does. link::#*eventControls:: reads a spec through it, and so can a page drawing the lines.
argument:: spec
argument:: keys

METHOD:: eventControls
Set an event's attraction controls from a hit's spec (as link::#*resolve:: reads it): a key in the value mode gets its set and strength, every other key a strength 0; the time key's course (the hit's code::<key>0::, code::<key>1::, and its path's Env when curved) gives the progress controls. Returns the variant the hit needs: nil (no attraction), code::\A:: (at most the pitch warped), code::\AA:: (another key warped).
argument:: ev
argument:: spec
argument:: keys

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: at
x warped at strong::amount::.
argument:: x
argument:: amount

METHOD:: neighbours
The attractors around x, code::[a, b, wa, wb]::; nil for an empty set or outside a set that does not repeat.
argument:: x

METHOD:: nearest
argument:: x

METHOD:: valuesIn
The attractors within [lo, hi], ascending (code::[value, weight]:: pairs with strong::withWeights::).
argument:: lo
argument:: hi
argument:: withWeights

METHOD:: withinRange
The part of the set a course between lo and hi reaches, with the attractor beyond each side, as values that do not repeat.
argument:: lo
argument:: hi

METHOD:: progressAt
The warped index of a line whose driving coordinate runs straight from x0 to x1: how far the warp has gone from W(x0) to W(x1). An index outside 0..1, or a line within one plateau, is left as it is.
argument:: index
argument:: x0
argument:: x1
argument:: amount

METHOD:: crossings
The progress values where a curved course (an Env over the line) crosses the attractors, with their weights, between the ends weighted 0: code::[[u, w], ...]::.
argument:: env
argument:: samples

METHOD:: transpose
The same set moved (its root, or every value when it does not repeat).
argument:: by

METHOD:: degrees
METHOD:: period
METHOD:: root
METHOD:: weights
METHOD:: isPeriodic
METHOD:: name
METHOD:: copy

EXAMPLES::
code::
~a = RCAttractor.scale(Scale.major, weights: [3, 1, 1, 1, 2, 1, 1]);
~a.at(0.37, 0.6);                                   // drawn to the nearer degree
(0..20).collect { |i| ~a.at(i / 20, 0.9).round(0.001) };   // nearly steps
~a.progressAt(0.5, 0, 1, 0.6);                      // a line from pitch 0 to 1, halfway in time
RCAttractor.sieve(RCSieve.residues(12, [0, 3, 4, 6, 8, 9], 1/12)).degrees * 12;
// in a template: the controls a synth reads, and the variant it needs
RCAttractor.eventControls((pitch0: 0, pitch1: 1), (pitch: (set: Scale.dorian, amount: 0.7, mode: \both)), [\pitch]);
::
